# 🐱 CAT — SPARSE NEURAL CODING

## Architecture
```
Cat visual cortex uses SPARSE CODING.
Only ~1% of neurons active at any time.
Maximum information with minimum energy.
Evolved for hunting efficiency.
```

## Biological Mechanism
```
SPARSE CODING PRINCIPLE:

Visual scene → Sparse representation
10,000 possible neurons
Only ~100 active for any input
Compression ratio: 100:1

ADVANTAGES:
- Energy efficient (1% activation)
- Noise resistant (specific patterns)
- Fast pattern matching (few comparisons)
- High storage capacity (orthogonal codes)
```

