# 🐝 BEE — SWARM INTELLIGENCE

## Architecture
```
Bee colonies are superorganisms.
Individual bees have ~1M neurons.
Colony has ~60 billion neurons (1000 workers × 60K each).
Collective intelligence emerges from simple rules.
```

## Biological Mechanism
```
SWARM DECISION MAKING:

1. Scouts find options
2. Report via waggle dance
3. Quality encoded in dance duration
4. Bees follow highly-advertised options
5. Quorum sensing determines threshold
6. Colony decides when quorum reached

QUORUM THRESHOLD: ~20-30 bees at site
DECISION TIME: Hours to days
ACCURACY: >90% optimal choice
```

