# 🐙 OCTOPUS — DISTRIBUTED PROCESSING

## Architecture
```
Octopuses have 9 brains.
1 central brain + 8 arm brains.
2/3 of neurons in arms.
Each arm can act semi-independently.
```

## Biological Mechanism
```
DISTRIBUTED ARCHITECTURE:

Central brain: High-level coordination
Arm brains: Local processing + action

Arms can:
- Solve problems independently
- Taste, touch, decide locally
- Coordinate without central command

PARALLEL PROCESSING: 8 independent units
```

