# 🐬 DOLPHIN — CONTINUOUS CONSCIOUSNESS

## Architecture
```
Dolphins have unihemispheric sleep.
One brain hemisphere sleeps while other stays awake.
Never fully unconscious.
Always aware, always present.
```

## Biological Mechanism
```
UNIHEMISPHERIC SLEEP:

Left hemisphere sleeps → Right controls
Right hemisphere sleeps → Left controls
Alternating: ~2 hours per side

ALWAYS CONSCIOUS: No full sleep state
ECHOLOCATION: Continuous environmental awareness
